title ALES207 — Lotus's stereo reverb early/late balance, the first reflections against the diffuse wash per ear
prompt recur loop — continue the Lotus/ALES ladder Lindy-first crux-first, each finished rung its own signed round pushed to origin and xykj61, stop at the custody gates
think ALES206 gave the mono reverb its early/late balance; the ladder always closes the mono/stereo pair before opening a fresh axis, so the thin twin is stereo_reverb_early_late — the same crossfade over both channels of a StereoClip, one shared early bank/room/balance, the image held. Mirrored ALES193 (stereo_reverb_mix) exactly, swapping the dry snapshot for the EARLY reflections (ALES69 multitap_ms per channel on a copy) and the wet for the LATE preset (ALES191 stereo_reverb_preset in place).
think No stereo timed multi-tap exists (only ALES183 stereo_multitap, index-named), so the early half runs ALES69's proven multitap_ms once per channel on the copy — the mono discipline twice, exactly ALES183's own argument, each channel reading its own dry, no cross-channel snapshot. StereoReverbEarlyLateError = multitap_time.MultitapTimeError || stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || BadBalance; the early multi-tap on the copy and the late preset's precheck keep the master untouched on any refusal (atomic).
obs Witness GREEN on the first metal pass — no RED to book. Six laws on a 1024-sample bench with two distinct impulses: the early edge per channel equals multitap_ms over the room's published early bank byte for byte; the late edge equals stereo_reverb_preset byte for byte on both channels; a half balance differs from both edges and each sample of each channel is the honest weighted average, byte for byte; the image is held (centred identical, stereo distinct — no crossing); the channels leave balanced and silence stays silence; faults forward atomic (BadBalance, DurationTooLong, BadRange, both channels untouched). ALES191 stereo preset, ALES69 multi-tap, and ALES206 mono early/late all re-run GREEN beside it; TAME bans clean, width exit 0. The early/late axis now stands whole for mono and stereo.
